       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults in a monitored setting, which is 3,200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory dose\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum daily dose\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, a typical analgesic dose\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it is intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
